so we've been talking about the  anti-vaccine movement for I don't even  know four years since Pat was a little  kid at this point I think is fair to say  but we've been talking about it a lot in  2019 as well because the World Health  Organization has actually listed anti  vaccine sentiment as one of the top 10  global health threats of 2019 and the  reason that it is now a world health  threat rather than just the US is that  there are sort of nodes of anti vaccine  sentiment in the broader anti-vaxxer  network all over the world so in the  u.s. you've got Oregon and Washington  you've got a particular part of North  Carolina that is plagued for not using a  pun but it's plagued by anti vaccine  sentiment Italy has been a focal point  Japan we talked about last week or the  week before we talked last week about  Waterloo Ontario and Canada there's many  of these nodes in the anti-vaxxer  Network and I'm not going to bore you by  rehashing every single one of the  stories that we've done from each of  those places but I do have a new one to  add for you today which is from Italy  Italy has a I think it's not an  exaggeration to say a large anti-vaxxer  yet vaccination rate according to the  World Health Organization is 95% Italy  actually got down to 80% at one point in  time before they decided it's time for  us to take some action here 95% is  important because you need 95% for herd  immunity to function properly and the  concept of herd immunity I know a lot of  people know this is that when enough  people are vaccinated even unvaccinated  people are mostly protected because you  have most people protected which  disrupts the chain of infection and it  makes it mathematically unlikely that  someone who's unvaccinated because of a  medical condition for example or for  whatever reason will come in contact  with someone who is infectious and pass  along the disease that's the sort of  concept of herd immunity Italy has now  banned children under  from public schools in Italy unless they  have valid exemptions from vaccinations  if you send your unvaccinated kid to  school who's between the ages of 6 and  16 you can be fined up to 500 euro which  is about 560 dollars at today's exchange  rate and this is all because of  something called the Lorenz in law the  Lorenzen law says that children who go  to public school must receive vaccines  for chickenpox polio measles mumps and  rubella before they are allowed to  attend school and since the law was  introduced vaccination rates have  actually started to rise again from that  roughly 80% bottom out rate which is  really bad I mean that means one out of  five kids is not vaccinated you're not  even close to herd immunity at that rate  and now Italy is saying stop sending the  unvaccinated children to school so once  again they're sort of like two  categories kids up to six years old and  kids between 6 and 16 if you are six or  under you can't go to school without  proof of vaccination period if you are 6  to 16 you're not banned but your parents  get fined and 500 euro is a it's not  nothing let's put it that way  different regions of Italy are sort of  handling the law differently in bologna  letters of suspension have been sent to  300 children some other areas have  extended a grace period and you know  every time we talk about this pat we  start getting there's like I don't know  three or four different categories of  emails that we get we will get the  emails that focus on what they believe  is the lack of safety of the vaccines  themselves they say the vaccines  themselves are harmful sometimes they  will say they cause autism etc then you  have those who focus instead on the sort  of government mandate element of it's  saying governments can't  or at least shouldn't be mandating  specific medical treatments vaccines  being part of that and every time I  think it's important to mention Pat this  does not say that vaccination is in and  of itself mandatory it  mandatory if you want to send your kids  to public school if you want to  home-school them or send them to a  private school that doesn't have these  requirements with peace and love go  ahead and do that but this is not a  mandate that you have to vaccinate it's  the decision that if you want your kids  in public school  they must be vaccinated yeah and I think  that makes perfect sense because when  you decide to put your kids in public  schools you're giving up some of your  rights I mean you're taking part in  society and that's kind of what goes  along with it you have to follow certain  rules if you don't want to follow those  rules as you say you can homeschool your  kids you can put them into private  schools if you can afford it hopefully  it doesn't come to that hopefully these  anti-vaxxer parents will just cave and  get their children vaccinated and put  them in public schools so yes it doesn't  pin John people's freedoms but I think  in a totally reasonable way maybe  eventually we'll get to the point where  the anti-vaxxer movement has spread so  significantly that we'd have to talk  about mandatory vaccines for everyone  not just as it applies to public schools  but I hope we don't get to that point  because that would be a tough decision  to make yeah and it would be it was  legally problematic I mean it would be  different in different countries based  on how the law and constitutions when  they exist are written but I mean listen  we should not be in a situation where  that's even necessary let let's just  that we need an education campaign we  need to sort of take back the the the  misinformation that is being spread by  these anti vaccine errs and I hesitate  to even mention this other bit of news  but in the meantime yet another research  paper indicates that vaccines don't  cause autism and what I mean by I  hesitate to mention it is I don't even  want to admit to myself that this is  still something that has to be talked  about but I still get emails from people  saying vaccines specifically the MMR  vaccine causes autism we now have one  paper from dr. Andrew Wakefield who lost  his medical license a paper that has  been debunked because of its bad science  that says MMR is linked to autism and  now you have I don't even know how many  papers multiple serious research studies  including yet another one from the last  week or two which says there is  absolutely no evidence that the MMR  vaccine  causes autism in children or in anybody  and I've mentioned before that there is  left-wing and right-wing anti-vaxxer ISM  and for different reasons they've sort  of joined forces on the left you have  skepticism of Big Pharma catalyzing a  lot of anti VAX sentiment on the right  you have skepticism of government  catalyzing and coalescing some of that  anti VAX sentiment and you have overlap  people on the left and right saying I  absolutely agree with you about vaccines  being bad  but for completely different reasons and  it's interesting to see but interesting  is sort of the wrong term to apply  because it's also so so so destructive  and we will we'll see what happens with  the vaccination rate in Italy and we  will continue to follow this movement in  2019 which again was listed by the World  Health Organization as one of the  largest ten health threats it's optional  it's completely optional and yet it is a  serious health threat to humans

